# pstack → herdr agent routing. One line per pstack role/task key.
# Shape mirrors ~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc (role → model), but values are
# herdr agent kinds (agy, claude, …) or routing aliases.
#
# Philosophy (arena / interrogate / poteto):
# - Model diversity for judgment stays on Cursor Task (pstack-models) — NEVER fake it with N×same herdr kind.
# - Arena Frame→Fan→Cross-judge→Pick→Graft→Verify and Interrogate reviewers stay `local`.
# - Herd/herdr only after Act-on for session-sized *implement* arms (separate worktrees).
# - Prove-it, propose, merge stay local (fleet authority).
#
# Values:
#   <kind>              — Herd spawns interactive herdr agent (registry Status must be ready)
#   kind1, kind2        — ordered preference; first ready wins
#   local | pstack-task | inherit-parent — do NOT route to herdr
#
# Companion twin: copy references/pstack-herdr-agents.md beside the rule
# Registry gate: operator registry (see references/registry.example.md)
# Orch skill: herd-with-herdr

# --- Session-sized implement (herdr workhorse) ---
feature, refactoring: agy
bug-fix: agy
perf-issue: agy
swarm workers: agy
openspec-apply, session-apply: agy
arena-implement-arm: agy

# --- Judgment / hardest / hillclimb (pstack Task models — not herdr) ---
hardest tasks: local
hillclimb: local
judgment and prose: local
how explorer: local
how explainer: local
how critics: local
why investigators: local
why synthesizer: local
reflect tooling: local
reflect judgment, divergent, synthesizer: local

# --- Arena / interrogate / architect panels (ALWAYS local until true kind diversity exists) ---
# Do not map these to agy. One kind ≠ arena. Cross-judge is never a herdr agent.
arena runners: local
arena cross-judge pool: local
architect runners: local
interrogate reviewers: local

# --- Fleet authority (never external) ---
openspec-propose: local
eng-lead-merge: local
prove-it: local
